afk: the scoped re-review dispatches the `reviewer` agent, not a model.

Motivation: the task tool has no model parameter (agent types instead),
reviews always take `reviewer`, and reports live at `local://` so an
isolated fixer's report survives outside its snapshot.

What must survive a rebase:
- No [MODEL] placeholder; `reviewer` agent stated instead.
- [REPORT_URI] (local://) replaces [REPORT_FILE]; brief referenced by
  repo-relative path.
- Re-review range is the fix's own parked ref
  (merge-base HEAD <fixref> .. <fixref>), not FIX_BASE..HEAD.
- Tests section assumes test-first fix rounds (see
  skills-sdd-fixer-prompt.patch): the re-review demands per-finding RED
  evidence — the failing run before the fix — or an accepted
  `NOT TESTABLE: <why>` justification, and a green-only regression test
  verdicts NOT ADDRESSED.
- Finding Verdicts cite the RED evidence alongside file:line.

